            <h1>Exercise Name: Seated Dumbbell Front Raises</h1>
           <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>

This is an isolation exercise focused on building strength and size in the front portion of your shoulders.

 Primary Target Muscle: Anterior Deltoids (Front Delts)—highlighted in orange/yellow on the front of the shoulders in the animation.
 Secondary Muscles: Upper Chest (Clavicular Head of Pectoralis Major) and Serratus Anterior.

</div></div>
<pre>

<h1>How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1>

<u><b><h4>1. Starting Position</h4></b></u>:
 Sit upright on a flat or upright bench with your back straight and feet firmly planted on the floor.
 Hold a dumbbell in each hand with an overhand grip (palms facing your thighs) resting by your sides.


<u><b><h4>2. The Execution (Raise)</h4></b></u>:
 Exhale and slowly lift both dumbbells straight up in front of you until your arms are parallel to the floor (shoulder height).
 Maintain a slight, natural bend in your elbows; do not lock them out completely.
 Hold for a brief second at the top.


<u><b><h4>3. The Lowering Phase</h4></b></u>:
 Inhale and gradually lower the dumbbells back down under full control to the starting position.





<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Front Shoulder Hypertrophy:</b> Directly targets and builds the front deltoids for full, rounded shoulder caps.
 <b>◉Improved Overhead Pressing:</b> Builds foundational strength for functional pushing movements and heavy overhead presses.
 <b>◉Strict Form:</b> Performing this movement seated prevents momentum or swinging your body, forcing the shoulders to do all the work.



<h1>Recommended Sets & Repetitions</h1>

| Fitness Level | Sets | Repetitions | Rest Period |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Beginner | 3 Sets | 12 – 15 Reps | 45–60 sec |
| Intermediate / Advanced | 3 – 4 Sets | 10 – 12 Reps | 60 sec |

> Pro Tip: Keep your core engaged and avoid leaning back as you lift the weights. If you find yourself arching your back, switch to a lighter weight.
